/Title (3. "The internet stops whenever the router is restarted": The single consumer home router acts as a single point of failure \(SPOF\) for NAT, DHCP, and WAN routing. When restarted, all active NAT translation tables are flushed, internal DHCP leases cannot renew, and there is no redundant gateway or failover path.)
