/Title (Mixed T568A/T568B Patch Cables: Wiring one end to T568A and the other to T568B swaps Tx pairs \(1,2\) with Rx pairs \(3,6\), creating an Ethernet crossover cable. Modern Gigabit Ethernet switches \(1000BASE-T and IEEE 802.3ab\) mandate Auto-MDIX, which automatically detects the crossover wiring and swaps Tx/Rx electronically, so modern switches still operate normally. However, all patch cables should be re-terminated to uniform T568B for standards compliance and troubleshooting clarity.)
